    (v_topic_id, 'A 72-year-old female is brought to the clinic after her bank flagged multiple late mortgage payments and several unusual wire transfers to unverified overseas accounts. The patient, who previously managed all household finances, admits she now finds balancing the checkbook confusing and has been paying bills twice or not at all. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?', '["Perform cognitive testing (e.g., MoCA) to screen for cognitive impairment, and advise the family to establish a durable power of attorney (POA) for finances to protect the patient from financial exploitation", "File a mandatory elder abuse report against the bank for flagging the patient''s accounts", "Immediately prescribe a cholinesterase inhibitor to reverse the financial errors", "Advise the patient to close all bank accounts and carry only cash to simplify transactions", "Recommend immediate nursing home placement as the patient is incapable of independent living"]'::jsonb, 0, 'Financial management (Accounting) is a complex IADL that requires intact executive functioning. Deficits in managing finances are often the **earliest sign of cognitive decline** or dementia (e.g., Alzheimer''s). The clinician must perform formal cognitive testing (like the Montreal Cognitive Assessment [MoCA]) to evaluate the underlying cause and counsel the family to secure financial protections (such as establishing a financial Durable Power of Attorney [POA] or a co-signer) to prevent financial exploitation, scams, and unpaid bills. (Ref: Hazzard''s Ch. 12, Ch. 72)'),
    (v_topic_id, 'A 89-year-old male is brought to the clinic after his bank flagged multiple late mortgage payments and several unusual wire transfers to unverified overseas accounts. The patient, who previously managed all household finances, admits he now finds balancing the checkbook confusing and has been paying bills twice or not at all. Which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management?', '["Immediately prescribe a cholinesterase inhibitor to reverse the financial errors", "Perform cognitive testing (e.g., MoCA) to screen for cognitive impairment, and advise the family to establish a durable power of attorney (POA) for finances to protect the patient from financial exploitation", "Advise the patient to close all bank accounts and carry only cash to simplify transactions", "Recommend immediate nursing home placement as the patient is incapable of independent living", "File a mandatory elder abuse report against the bank for flagging the patient''s accounts"]'::jsonb, 1, 'Financial management (Accounting) is a complex IADL that requires intact executive functioning. Deficits in managing finances are often the **earliest sign of cognitive decline** or dementia (e.g., Alzheimer''s). The clinician must perform formal cognitive testing (like the Montreal Cognitive Assessment [MoCA]) to evaluate the underlying cause and counsel the family to secure financial protections (such as establishing a financial Durable Power of Attorney [POA] or a co-signer) to prevent financial exploitation, scams, and unpaid bills. (Ref: Hazzard''s Ch. 12, Ch. 72)'),
